{"title":"datasette-cluster-map 0.19","link":"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/13/datasette-cluster-map/","date":1794610965000,"content":"\n    \n        <p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/datasette-cluster-map/releases/tag/0.19\">datasette-cluster-map 0.19</a></p>\n        <p>One of the oldest Datasette plugins, and still one of my favorites. It now works with Datasette 1.0a42, and depends on <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/13/datasette-leaflet/\">the new datasette-leaflet</a> to ensure OpenStreetMap tiles are requested with a referrer header.</p>\n<p>Here's <a href=\"https://datasette.io/global-power-plants/global-power-plants?owner=Pacific+Gas+%26+Electric+Co.\">a map of power plants owned by California's PG&amp;E</a>, also demonstrating Datasette's recently <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/datasette/pull/3032\">redesigned facets</a>:</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Screenshot of a faceted map interface. Three facet panels at the top: &quot;country_long 1&quot; with United States of America 81 selected; &quot;owner 1&quot; with Pacific Gas &amp; Electric Co. 81 selected; &quot;primary_fuel 5&quot; listing Hydro 63, Solar 10, Gas 5, Storage 2, Nuclear 1. Each primary_fuel row has a pale blue horizontal bar behind its label, sized in proportion to its count: Hydro's bar fills most of the row width, Solar's is a short sliver, Gas's is shorter still, and Storage and Nuclear have only a thin strip at the left edge. Below is a Leaflet map with + and − zoom controls showing California and Nevada, with marker clusters across northern and central California: 9 near Redding, 21 near Chico, 2 to the west of Chico, 13 northeast of Sacramento, 7 east of Stockton, 6 at Oakland, 10 at Fresno, 9 west of Visalia, 2 north of Bakersfield, plus two individual blue pin markers on the coast, one in the far north and one north of Santa Maria. Attribution: Leaflet | © OpenStreetMap contributors\" src=\"/media/c9f57c1dd25b2a5f970770de087c2f6dc4fa0439c2b1227d24f3ad592adbd723.webp\" /></p>\n    \n    \n        <p>Tags: <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/datasette\">datasette</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/geospatial\">geospatial</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/openstreetmap\">openstreetmap</a></p>\n    \n\n","author":"Simon Willison","siteTitle":"Simon Willison’s Weblog","siteHash":"1b599216bd27a00f15d67a3ed9719c64148630c70244b6dd8e743f17cb45527e","entryHash":"c1dcb1d916ade71b7eacc59658c496c099226e454be9f499183b32f9b16cfe93","category":"Tech"}